Ladybird uses a video element for application/ogg because the container
can hold video or just audio. Blink and WebKit create a video element in
MediaDocumentParser, and Gecko does so in
VideoDocument::CreateVideoElement.

Chrome 158.0.8127.37, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 used a video
element with controls for both audio-only and video Ogg containers
served as application/ogg. Their codec support differed. Ladybird
decoded both samples and displayed the video at its intrinsic width.
